P02.02.02 — replace the stub `workspace` gate with the QG-01 gate set and add `stress`.

This file is founder-only (.claude/policy/protected-paths.json), so this session
wrote the change as a patch instead of editing it. Apply it yourself:

    git apply docs/control-plane/patches/0003-p02-gates.patch
    python3 .claude/bin/control_plane_check.py
    python3 .claude/bin/gates.py full

What changes
------------
Removed: the `workspace` stub (`pnpm turbo run lint typecheck test build`), which
existed only so that `full` could not pass before P02 landed.

Added, in QG-01's order (PLAN.md, Cross-Phase Quality Gates):

  conventions   Conventional Commit + no-attribution self-tests (P02.01.03)
  format        prettier --check
  lint          turbo run lint (includes the two repository rules)
  boundaries    dependency-cruiser (P02.02.07)
  typecheck     turbo run typecheck
  unit          turbo run test
  integration   turbo run test:integration   [requires docker]
  build         turbo run build
  secret-scan   gitleaks over history

`fast` becomes control-plane, conventions, format, lint, typecheck, unit — the
loop that needs no Docker.

`stress` is added (20 iterations of `pnpm exec vitest run {targets}`), which
`gates.py stress --targets` needs and which the stub had no section for.

Not yet included, with the phase that adds them
-----------------------------------------------
  RLS catalog check + cross-tenant suite   P06.02, P06.03
  OpenAPI + client drift                   P06, P07
  migration safety check                   P02.06.04 wires it into CI; it is
                                           added here once packages/db exists
  dependency audit + licence check         P02.08

Each is a tightening, which needs no approval; they land with the phase that
makes them real rather than as a gate that passes because it checks nothing.

Note
----
`integration` requires Docker. On a machine without a reachable daemon that gate
is reported SKIPPED-UNVERIFIED rather than passing, so a skip can never be read
as a pass.

